[?9001h[?1004h[?25l[2J[m[H]0;claude[?25h[?2004h[?2031h[?1004h]0;✳ Claude Code[?1049h[2J[?1000h[?1002h[?1003h[?1006h[?2026h[?2026l[?25l[48;2;55;55;55m  [38;2;153;153;153mfor my answer.                                                                                                                                                                    [39m  [38;2;153;153;153m- If I decline, end your turn with a single line saying we are going straight to planning — again a statement, not a question.                                                    [39m  [38;2;153;153;153m- If I accept, do STEP 4.                                                                                                                                                         [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;153;153;153mSTEP 4 — Write the design brief, and STOP. Do NOT try to run the `design` skill yourself: it is reserved for explicit user invocation and the Skill tool will refuse it. I will   [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mrun it for you the moment your brief is on disk.                                                                                                                                  [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;153;153;153mWrite the brief to `plays/009-select-stop/design/brief.md` — one short paragraph on what the product is, who it is for and the look and feel it should have, then one line per    [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mnew screen naming it and saying what it does. Brief it from intent.md, the product vision and the tech stack, and look at the attached repositories first: if this product        [39m  [38;2;153;153;153malready has a frontend, say so and name its real colours, type and spacing so the design matches rather than inventing a new look. End the brief by saying the canvas payload     [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mmust be saved as `plays/009-select-stop/design/canvas.html`.                                                                                                                      [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;153;153;153mKeep it compact — it is passed to the design skill as a single line, so write it as flowing prose with no headings, no bullet characters and no code blocks. Then end your turn   [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mwith one short statement saying the brief is ready. NOT a question: that statement is what starts the design run.                                                                 [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;153;153;153mSTEP 5 — Once the design skill has produced the canvas, leave the design in two places, both of which matter:                                                                     [39m  [38;2;153;153;153m1. `plays/009-select-stop/design/design.md` — the published canvas URL, then one line per screen saying what it is and what it does. The Planner and the Developer read this      [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mfile; keep it short and factual.                                                                                                                                                  [39m  [38;2;153;153;153m2. `documentation/design/009-select-stop-prototype.html` — how I actually LOOK at the prototype, from the Documentation tab of the project screen. Create the folder if it is not [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mthere. This file is rendered inside a sandboxed iframe with NO scripting, NO navigation and NO network, so it must be ONE self-contained page: every artboard's markup stacked    [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mone under another with a heading naming the screen, every style inline or in a `<style>` block in that same file, no script tags, and no references to any external file, font or [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mimage (inline any image as a data URI). Put the canvas URL at the top as plain visible text as well as a link — a link alone cannot be opened from that sandbox. Do NOT copy the  [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mcanvas payload itself here; it needs JavaScript and would render as a blank page.                                                                                                 [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;153;153;153mIf the canvas cannot be PUBLISHED, that is fine: keep the artboards the skill produced, still write both documents from them, and say plainly that the canvas was not published.  [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mThat is the only fallback. If the design skill did not run at all, do NOT hand-write a canvas file or a prototype in its place — say plainly that the skill did not run and stop, [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mso the problem is visible instead of being papered over with something that only looks like a design.                                                                             [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;153;153;153mSTEP 6 — Hand the prototype to me for review, and STOP. Once both documents are written, end your turn by telling me in a few lines what you designed and where I can look at it, [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mand then ASKING me to review the prototype and confirm it is what I want before you plan the implementation. End that turn on that question and wait — planning does not start    [39m  [38;2;153;153;153muntil I have approved the design.                                                                                                                                                 [39m  [38;2;153;153;153m- If I ask for changes, revise the design and both documents, then ask me again. Keep ending those turns on a question.                                                           [39m  [38;2;153;153;153m- Only once I have actually approved it, end your turn with a single short statement saying the design is approved. That statement — and nothing else — is what starts the        [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mplanning session. Never write it while I still owe you an answer.                                                                                                                 [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;153;153;153mYou are designing only. Do not modify anything in the repositories, do not implement anything, and do not write `plays/009-select-stop/plan.md`.                                  [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;153;153;153mPROJECT CONTEXT FILES: this project keeps its documentation under `documentation/`; the documents in `documentation/context/` are shared by every play and apply to all work.     [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mRead ALL of them before doing anything and make your work conform to them: `documentation/context/vision.md` (the problem, users, and product direction),                         [39m  [38;2;153;153;153m`documentation/context/tech.md` (overall architecture plus the technology used in each repository). Only the Architect writes `documentation/context/vision.md` and               [39m  [38;2;153;153;153m`documentation/context/tech.md`; treat every other document as read-only reference the user maintains, and do not create, move or edit anything under `documentation/` EXCEPT     [39m  [38;2;153;153;153m`documentation/design/`, which is yours to write in this session.                                                                                                                 [m
